<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Intentionally empty for the ad-hoc dev build.

      `com.apple.developer.applesignin` is a restricted entitlement: macOS's
      AppleMobileFileIntegrity daemon (amfid) rejects ad-hoc-signed bundles
      that claim it, which manifests as `launchd job spawn failed`
      (POSIX 163) at launch time.

      Apple Sign-In requires a Developer ID-signed bundle anyway, so leaving
      the entitlement out costs nothing on the ad-hoc dev path. When you
      enroll in the Apple Developer Program and switch to a Developer ID
      identity, add the entitlement back here — and only then will codesign
      accept it.

      Google OAuth (the current sign-in path) doesn't need any restricted
      entitlement; it only needs the custom URL scheme registered in
      Info.plist for the OAuth redirect.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
